    {q:"Describe how a hill looks different from a mountain.",memo:"A hill is raised land that is usually lower and less steep than a mountain. A mountain rises steeply and often has a peak.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["lower|smaller|shorter|less steep|gentle|rounded|round|not as high|not as steep|not as tall"]},{"kw":["peak|steep|taller|higher|bigger|pointed|steeper|high"]}]}},
    {q:"A learner says: “A plain is a deep narrow valley with steep sides.” Correct this statement, and say what a plateau is.",memo:"A plain is a large area of mostly flat or gently rolling land. A plateau is high land with a relatively flat top.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["flat|gently|rolling|wide|open|large|level"]},{"kw":["high|raised|top|table"]}]}},
    {q:"Define erosion. Does erosion break rock down in the place where it is found? Explain.",memo:"Erosion is the wearing away and movement of soil, sand and rock from one place to another. No – breaking rock down in the place where it is found is weathering.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["move|moving|carry|carried|transport|wear|wearing|taken|washes|moves|carries|one place to another"]},{"kw":["no$|not|doesnt|does not|never|weathering|moves|carried away|takes away"]}]}},
