    {q:"Explain why a rock in a desert, which is very hot by day and very cold at night, may eventually crack.",memo:"The rock expands when it heats up in the day and contracts when it cools at night. Repeating this over time makes cracks grow until the rock breaks.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["expand|swell|bigger|larger|get hot|heats up|heat up|grow"]},{"kw":["contract|shrink|smaller|cool down|cools down|gets cold"]}]}},
