    {q:"Name the THREE natural agents that can cause erosion, and explain how ONE of them wears away or moves sediment.",memo:"Water, wind and moving ice. Example: flowing water carries soil and rock away; wind lifts loose sand; moving ice scrapes the ground and carries rock.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["water|rain|river"]},{"kw":["wind"]},{"kw":["ice|glacier|snow"]},{"kw":["carry|carries|carried|move|moves|moved|wash|washes|blow|blows|scrape|scrapes|wear|wears|lift|lifts|push|pushes|erode"]}]}},
    {q:"Rainwater runs down a steep hillside with no plants on it and carries soil away. Name the process and explain why the bare hillside makes it worse.",memo:"Water erosion. Plant roots hold soil in place and slow the water; on a bare hillside nothing holds the soil, so it is easily washed away.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["erosion|erode|eroded"]},{"kw":["hold|holds|held|root|anchor|protect|cover|bind|grip|stay|keeps|keep|stop|nothing|slow|slows|absorb|soak"]}]}},
    {q:"Over a very long time, how can flowing water change the shape of a riverbank?",memo:"The river erodes the bank, carrying soil and rock away, so the bank can be cut back and the river can widen or change course.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["erode|erosion|wear|carry|carries|carried|washes|cut|cuts|cutting|remove|moves|take|takes|wash"]},{"kw":["deep|wide|bigger|larger|carv|shape|change|bend|curve"]}]}},
    {q:"What happens during deposition? Name TWO places where sediment may be deposited.",memo:"In deposition, moving water, wind or ice drops the sediment it has been carrying. Any two: river bends, river mouths, lakes, the seabed.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["drop|dropped|dump|settle|settles|leave|left|put down|collects|builds up"]},{"kw":["bend","mouth","lake","sea|seabed|ocean","delta|dam|riverbed|river"],"min":2}]}},
