    {q:"Put these in the correct order and name each process: (a) the loose pieces are carried down the river, (b) the pieces drop onto the river bed, (c) a cliff face cracks into small pieces.",memo:"First (c) – weathering; then (a) – erosion; then (b) – deposition. (Order and all three names needed.)",r:{"order":["weathering","erosion","deposition"]}},
    {q:"A river runs through a mountain gorge. Explain how weathering, erosion and deposition work together to change the gorge over many years.",memo:"Weathering breaks rock on the gorge walls into pieces; the river erodes and carries the pieces downstream; where the water slows, the sediment is deposited. Together, over many years, these processes change the shape of the gorge.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["break|breaks|crack|smaller pieces|pieces"]},{"kw":["carr|wash|move|transport|take|taken|flow"]},{"kw":["settle|drop|dump|slow|collect|build up|left|pile|stop"]},{"kw":["deeper|wider|shape|carve|cut|bigger"]}]}},
