  "t4-nst-2": [
    {q:"What is sediment? Give TWO examples.",memo:"Sediment is small pieces of rock, minerals or organic material. Examples: sand, mud, small rock fragments, remains of living things.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["small|tiny|little|bits|pieces|particles|fragments|grains"]},{"kw":["sand","mud","silt","clay","gravel|pebble|stone|fragment|rock pieces|rocks","remains|shell|dead|plant|animal|organic|living","soil"],"min":2}]}},
    {q:"Write the five stages that turn rock into new sedimentary rock, in the correct order.",memo:"Weathering → erosion → deposition → compaction → cementation.",r:{"order":["weathering|weather","erosion|erode","deposition|deposit|settl","compaction|compact","cementation|cement"]}},
    {q:"In sedimentary rock formation, what happens during compaction?",memo:"The weight of the upper layers presses the lower layers of sediment together.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["weight|heavy|press|squash|squeez|pressure|push|compress|crush"]},{"kw":["layer|sediment|grain|above|top|lower|bottom|together|rock"]}]}},
    {q:"In sedimentary rock formation, what happens during cementation?",memo:"Minerals between the grains help to bind (glue) the sediment together into rock.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["mineral|glue|stick|bind|bond|join|hold|gum|paste"]},{"kw":["together|grains|particles|sediment|pieces|rock"]}]}},
    {q:"A learner says: “Shale forms in one day when mud dries out.” Explain why this is wrong.",memo:"Shale forms over a very long time, as very fine mud builds up in layers and is slowly compacted and cemented.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["long|years|millions|thousands|slow|slowly|time|ages|centur"]},{"kw":["layer|build up|builds|press|compact|cement|pile|pressure"]}]}},
    {q:"Explain why the lowest layers of sediment in a cliff are pressed together harder than the layers higher up.",memo:"The lower layers carry the weight of all the layers above them, so they are pressed together harder.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["weight|heavy|heavier|pressure|squash|squeez|crush"]},{"kw":["above|on top|more layers|more sediment|pile|stack|layers on|top of|piled"]}]}},
