    {q:"Describe one difference in the chores or expectations some boys and girls are given in some families, and explain why unfair differences should change.",memo:"Example: in some families girls are expected to cook and clean while boys play outside. Unfair differences should change because they limit people’s opportunities; everyone deserves equal chances and respect.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["cook|clean|sweep|chore|herd|fetch|sport|soccer|cattle|garden|wash|babysit|dishes|care for|look after|wood|water|work|jobs|laundry|outside|inside"]},{"kw":["equal|fair|limit|everyone|opportunit|respect|rights|choice|anyone|talent|abilit|can do|both|same chances|not right|hurt|stop"]}]}},
    {q:"Name ONE South African woman or women’s group who helped to change South Africa, and describe what she or they did.",memo:"Accept any accurate example, e.g. Charlotte Maxeke (founded the Bantu Women’s League); Lilian Ngoyi, Helen Joseph, Rahima Moosa and Sophie de Bruyn (leaders of the 1956 Women’s March to the Union Buildings); Albertina Sisulu.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["maxeke|sisulu|ngoyi|helen joseph|rahima|sophie|winnie|madikizela|makeba|womens march|1956|union buildings|bantu women|fatima meer|kuzwayo|dlamini zuma|madonsela|ramphele|moosa|bruyn"]},{"kw":["led|lead|march|fight|fought|free|equal|rights|start|found|first|degree|doctor|nurse|teach|protest|petition|stood|help|apartheid|league|movement|campaign|organis|leader|brave|speak|spoke|against|support"]}]}},
    {q:"Give TWO examples of work or roles in which women help to develop their local communities.",memo:"Any two: nurses or doctors (health care); teachers; business owners who create jobs; community leaders; leaders of social movements.",r:{"kw":["nurse|doctor|health|hospital|medical|clinic","teach|school|educat|principal","business|company|ceo|entrepreneur|shop|jobs|owner|sell","leader|community|ward|councillor|mayor|politic|minister|president|premier|speak","farm|garden|food|grow|crops","care|family|children|raise|home","movement|march|rights|fight|activist|protest|campaign"],"min":2}},
    {q:"Give a reasoned opinion: why is it good for a school or community when girls and boys are given equal chances to lead? Give TWO reasons.",memo:"Accept reasoned answers, e.g. more skills and ideas are used; decisions are fairer; everyone feels respected and able to contribute; problems get solved faster.",r:{"kw":["skills|talent|ideas|abilities|different|strengths|knowledge","fair|equal|respect|rights|treated","solve|problem|better decisions|decision|progress|develop|grow|succeed|work together|together|teamwork","jobs|economy|money|income|business","role model|inspire|example|children|young"],"min":2}},
    {q:"Name the Hindu festival known as the ‘Festival of Lights’ and explain what it celebrates.",memo:"Diwali. It celebrates the triumph of light over darkness and good over evil.",r:{"all":[{"kw":["diwali|divali|deepavali"]},{"kw":["light|lamp|good|evil|dark|victory|triumph|win|overcome|beat"]}]}},
    {q:"Name TWO things people do or use to celebrate Diwali.",memo:"Any two: lighting clay lamps (diyas), making rangoli patterns, sharing sweets, family gatherings, fireworks.",r:{"kw":["lamp|diya|candle|light","rangoli|pattern|colour|colorful|floor","sweet|food|treat|mithai|feast|eat","firework|crackers|fire","family|gather|visit|friends|together","clean|new clothes|clothes|decorat|prayer|puja|lakshmi|gift"],"min":2}},
